  "closure_review": [
    "New hosted Kubernetes preflight uses urllib3 with existing public-address pinning and read-only request guard; no AWS SDK clients.",
    "GCP pagination and ECS/CloudFront inventory changes are collector execution paths; API only invokes credential factories and preflight.",
    "ACR descriptor occurrence validation and GKE image association/CDN reader changes do not introduce API SDK clients.",
    "Current source receipt transitions retain immutable source archives and before/after proof rows.",
    "Final correction: serialize only the shared collector registry import during concurrent cold preflights; cloud reads still overlap.",
    "Kubernetes pinned transport validates absolute origin using the existing guard, then sends only origin-form path/query to HTTPSConnectionPool.",
    "ACR per-reader transport admits one authenticated blob307 to exact public DNS-pinned AzureStorage host, forwards no registry credential, retains digest/size and redacted provenance; no SDK clients introduced."
  ],
